{
  "id": "staircase-method",
  "term": "staircase method",
  "definition": "In this context, a staircase method is a way of adjusting a perceptual task so objective accuracy is kept stable while other changes, such as perceptual thresholds or learning-related improvements, are measured. It is used to reduce the confounding effect of accuracy when studying metacognition or perceptual learning.",
